// A GENERIC BOUND OVER A PACKAGE-LOCAL HOMONYM TRAIT IS REFUSED AT THE BOUND.
//
// ⚠ LINK ORDER IS PART OF THE GROUND, AND THIS FILE STATES IT. Which of two
// same-name traits owns the BARE registry slot is decided by COLLECTION ORDER
// (B-mv-02 gives the slot to whoever is collected first). This fixture is
// SINGLE-TU with no `-l` archive, so the stdlib's `logos.lang.hash::Hash` is
// collected FIRST and owns the bare slot, and THIS package's `Hash` is the
// one pushed under its package-qualified key `trait_ident_homonym_bound_refused::Hash`.
// The diagnostic below names that qualified key, so the file also pins the
// direction of the collision — a different link order would move the slot and
// this test would not merely change message, it would be asking a different
// question. The MIRROR link order (an archive's homonym owning the bare slot)
// is `tests/logos/pass/trait_ident_pkg_chain.logos`, and it is NOT closed —
// see the note at the bottom.
//
// WHAT IS PINNED. `hmid_tag` is generic over THIS package's `Hash`. `i64`
// implements the STDLIB `Hash` and not this one, so `hmid_tag(5i64)` must be
// REFUSED, with a ground that says which trait the written name denotes and
// that the registry was searched under that identity.
//
// ⚠ WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT PIN. Before B-mv-03 this program compiled
// past sema and died in the MLIR verifier at
//     error: 'func.call' op 'i64__tag' does not reference a valid function
// — measured at 0236c697, rc 1. That string is the DEFECT, not the behaviour,
// and a `fail/` door holding it would be a green test asserting a defect. The
// expectation below is the sema REFUSAL and its ground; it cannot be satisfied
// by the verifier failure, which never mentions the trait at all.
//
// ⚠ THE REFUSAL MUST BE THE ONE WITH THE GROUND, NOT ANY REFUSAL. `fail/`
// matching is substring containment, so `.expected` carries the whole clause
// naming the qualified trait identity. A compiler that refused every `Hash`
// bound — the failure mode of a fix that dropped the local trait's impls
// instead of separating them — would not print that clause, and the LEGITIMATE
// direction is held green next door: `tests/logos/pass/trait_ident_homonym_bound.logos`
// still compiles and runs `call_marker(S{..})` and `S{..}.tag()` through this
// same package-local `Hash`. Both files must move together or the pair is lying.
package trait_ident_homonym_bound_refused;

extern fn printf(fmt: *const u8, ...) -> i32;

pub trait Hash { fn tag(&self) -> i64; }

pub struct S { pub a: i32, }
impl Hash for S { fn tag(&self) -> i64 { return 91i64; } }

// Generic over THIS package's Hash. Legitimate for S; refused for i64.
fn hmid_tag<T: Hash>(x: T) -> i64 { return x.tag(); }

fn main() -> i32 {
    let ok: i64 = hmid_tag(S { a: 1i32 });   // the legitimate direction
    let bad: i64 = hmid_tag(5i64);           // i64 implements the STDLIB Hash
    if ok != 91i64 { return 41; }
    if bad != 91i64 { return 42; }
    return 0i32;
}
